<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hop Depth Analysis</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Cross-Page Evidence Distribution Analysis ‣ 4.3. Breakdown Analysis ‣ 4. Results and Discussion ‣ BRIDGE: Benchmark for multi-hop Reasoning In long multimodal Documents with Grounded Evidence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows that performance remains comparable between 2-hop and 3+-hop questions for strong models, suggesting that hop depth alone does not fully determine difficulty. However, smaller models exhibit higher variance across hop bins.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7. </span>Performance by primary evidence modality (Text, Table, Figure), aggregated over prompting strategies. N denotes the number of instances whose dominant supporting evidence belongs to each modality.</figcaption>
